## 1. Utility — patient-days

`utility.gen()`: a CART model tries to tell real rows from synthetic rows. **S_pMSE** compares its
success with what chance gives: about 1 is ideal; below 3 is good, below 10 acceptable (Raab et al.).

```{r utility-rows, message = FALSE, warning = FALSE}
row_vars <- c("Days_since_bio", key_vars, covs, "resp_class_final")
# synthpop needs plain data.frames with factors; its list methods fail here, so each seed is run on its own
prep_rows <- function(d) as.data.frame(d[row_vars]) %>%
  mutate(sex_birth = factor(sex_birth), on_any_steroid = factor(on_any_steroid))
vae_rows   <- map(vae_list, prep_rows)
bench_rows <- map(bench_list, prep_rows)
real_rows  <- prep_rows(real)

ug_per_seed <- function(syn_list, real_df) {
  map_dfr(syn_list, function(s) {
    u <- utility.gen(s, real_df, method = "cart", print.flag = FALSE)
    tibble(pMSE = u$pMSE, S_pMSE = u$S_pMSE)
  }, .id = "seed")
}
ug_vae   <- ug_per_seed(vae_rows, real_rows)
ug_bench <- ug_per_seed(bench_rows, real_rows)

utility_overall <- bind_rows(`Temporal VAE` = ug_vae, `synthpop syn() (cross-sectional)` = ug_bench, .id = "method") %>%
  group_by(method) %>%
  summarise(pMSE = mean(pMSE), S_pMSE_mean = mean(S_pMSE), S_pMSE_min = min(S_pMSE), S_pMSE_max = max(S_pMSE),  # CHANGED: was S_pMSE = mean (overwrote it before min/max)
            .groups = "drop")
utility_overall
```

