## References

**Synthetic-data utility**

- Nowok, B., Raab, G. M., & Dibben, C. (2016). synthpop: Bespoke creation of synthetic data in R. *Journal of Statistical Software*, 74(11). https://www.jstatsoft.org/article/view/v074i11
- Raab, G. M., Nowok, B., & Dibben, C. Assessing, visualizing and improving the utility of synthetic data. arXiv:2109.12717. (The workflow used here: `utility.gen()` with CART, `compare()`, `utility.tables()`, thresholds 3 / 10.)
- Snoke, J., Raab, G. M., Nowok, B., Dibben, C., & Slavković, A. (2018). General and specific utility measures for synthetic data. *JRSS-A*, 181(3), 663–688. arXiv:1604.06651. (pMSE and the standardized S_pMSE.)
- Woo, M.-J., Reiter, J. P., Oganian, A., & Karr, A. F. (2009). Global measures of data utility for microdata masked for disclosure limitation. *Journal of Privacy and Confidentiality*, 1(1). (Origin of the propensity-score utility measure.)
- Karr, A. F., Kohnen, C. N., Oganian, A., Reiter, J. P., & Sanil, A. P. (2006). A framework for evaluating the utility of data altered to protect confidentiality. *The American Statistician*, 60(3), 224–232. (Confidence-interval overlap.)

**Generator (temporal VAE)**

- Kingma, D. P., & Welling, M. (2014). Auto-encoding variational Bayes. *ICLR*. arXiv:1312.6114.
